      "evidence": "The algorithm admits “consistent SPD matrices B₀,H₀” and says its matrix updates are interpreted over ℝ, then calls `alg-bfgs-hessian-direction-with-rounded-cholesky` on (Bₖ,gₖ). That procedure requires “representable finite entries” in its operationwise floating-point model. The admitted one-dimensional input B₀=√2, H₀=1/√2 is SPD and consistent but B₀ is not representable in any finite binary format, so a nonstationary rounded-mode run makes an undefined call immediately. Exact real updates also do not ensure later Bₖ remain representable.",
